1
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:19,228
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

2
00:00:19,311 --> 00:00:21,230
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

3
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:25,150
(DOOR RATTLES, CREAKS OPEN)

4
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:33,825
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

5
00:00:36,828 --> 00:00:38,497
- (GRUNTS)
- ♪ (MUSIC STOPS) ♪

6
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:41,792
What the fuck?

7
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:44,294
It's time to get up, Junior.

8
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:46,213
JOHN STEWART JUNIOR:
What did the Guardians say?

9
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:49,466
About what?

10
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:52,553
We got four dead aliens
on a football field.

11
00:00:52,636 --> 00:00:54,596
Another one just blew up
half the sheriff's station.

12
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:56,473
Oh yeah,
I'm not calling the Guardians.

13
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,267
JOHN: Then what the fuck
are you doing here, Hal?

14
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,060
- I'm training you.
- (BUCKET CLANGS)

15
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:01,562
(DOOR CLOSES)

16
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:04,982
(DOOR RATTLES)

17
00:01:07,943 --> 00:01:09,194
No, no, really.
You just take your time.

18
00:01:09,278 --> 00:01:10,445
What the fuck
are we doing, Jordan?

19
00:01:10,529 --> 00:01:12,281
What're you talking about?
You've been busting my balls

20
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:13,490
for a month to learn how to fly.

21
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,617
- Today's the day
you're gonna learn.
- We got a case to work.

22
00:01:15,701 --> 00:01:17,536
Jesus Christ Almighty.

23
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,162
Unclench.

24
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,040
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

25
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:27,713
You ready?

26
00:01:39,558 --> 00:01:42,144
(DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)

27
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:46,815
You fly.

28
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:47,899
Fly?

29
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,944
- Fly.
- (CHUCKLES)

30
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:53,447
(SCOFFS) That's it?
Just... just fly?

31
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,741
Oh, no, no, no, no.
I-- I-- I'm sorry.

32
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:57,075
- Fly, please.
- Ah.

33
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,827
HAL JORDAN: Look,
it's supposed to be instinctual.

34
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,621
Just concentrate.

35
00:02:00,704 --> 00:02:02,414
- Me, I'm a fighter pilot.
- JOHN: So I've heard.

36
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:04,207
When I think "fly,"
it's automatic.

37
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,626
See-- Just concentrate.

38
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,545
- Think flight.
- JOHN: Mm-hmm.

39
00:02:08,587 --> 00:02:09,921
Great. Thank you.

40
00:02:17,179 --> 00:02:18,472
Back up a little bit.

41
00:02:19,431 --> 00:02:22,392
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

42
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:33,111
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

43
00:02:36,907 --> 00:02:37,908
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

44
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,249
(INHALES DEEPLY)

45
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:47,417
(GRUNTS)

46
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:51,463
(RING WARBLING SOFTLY)

47
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:53,799
(BIRD CHIRPING)

48
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:55,592
(WINGS FLAPPING)

49
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:57,969
What the fuck is that?

50
00:02:59,054 --> 00:03:02,057
Uh, I think that's a bird, sir.

51
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,767
Uh...

52
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,727
Why don't you drop
the "sir" bullshit.

53
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:07,938
- We both know you don't mean it.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

54
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:08,980
Whatever you say.

55
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:10,607
(CHIRPING)

56
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:13,068
♪ (MUSIC FADING) ♪

57
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:16,196
- (RING PULSING)
- AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Ring nearing depletion.</i>

58
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:18,990
- All right, new lesson.
Gratis. Gimme the ring.
- (RING HUMS WEAKLY)

59
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:22,160
- Come on.
- (CHIRPING)

60
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,163
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

61
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,083
♪ (POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

62
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,334
Is there a problem?

63
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:33,797
- No. No.
- ♪ (BROODING STRING
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

64
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:37,134
Ring gets low on charge,
there's a...

65
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,802
(BIRD CHIRPING)

66
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,387
...one-time trick re-up.

67
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:43,348
You just gotta...

68
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,726
(CHIRPING)

69
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:48,770
Just gotta hit it flush.

70
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:51,940
- (RING HUMS SHARPLY)
- AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Ring charge, five percent.</i>

71
00:03:52,023 --> 00:03:54,151
- All right.
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

72
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:55,318
New flight plan.

73
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,613
- I booked you a window.
- I don't understand.

74
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:00,282
HAL: On an airplane.

75
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:02,242
There's seats near the windows,
there's seats near the aisles,

76
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,577
and there's seats
in the middle too.

77
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,495
Nobody wants those, uh--

78
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:08,999
Look, the point is I need
the lantern to charge the ring.

79
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,710
I need you
to go back to Coast City
to my place and get it.

80
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:14,171
The, uh, address is on the back
and the...

81
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:15,964
the key is out front
under the rock.

82
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:17,674
But, Hal,
this is already booked.

83
00:04:17,716 --> 00:04:19,718
- (BIRD CHIRPING)
- (WINGS FLAPPING)

84
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:21,678
Wait, so what would you
have done if I could fly?

85
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,889
Well, you didn't fly, did you?
So, it doesn't really matter.

86
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,891
Now get yourself ready.
I need that lantern.

87
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,310
Oh, uh...

88
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,855
One more thing.
Uh, feed Earl for me, would you?

89
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:34,691
- His food's in the icebox.
- And what's Earl?

90
00:04:34,775 --> 00:04:36,234
- Is it a dog? Cat?
- (CHIRPING)

91
00:04:36,318 --> 00:04:39,029
HAL: You know what?
And one more training exercise.

92
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:42,532
Take that... that bird with you
and bring it back alive.

93
00:04:42,574 --> 00:04:44,409
You lose concentration,
it disappears.

94
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:45,911
It disappears, you fail.

95
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,079
Don't fail.

96
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:50,707
(CHIRPING)

97
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,209
And what are you gonna be doing?

98
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,753
HAL: Enjoying
not answering your questions.

99
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:56,880
(DOOR CLOSES)

100
00:04:56,922 --> 00:05:02,969
♪ (BROODING GUITAR
RIFF PLAYING) ♪

101
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:13,939
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

102
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:19,236
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

103
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:38,463
♪ (BROODING MUSIC OVERLAPPING) ♪

104
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:58,024
(SPRINKLERS HISSING)

105
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:03,488
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

106
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,423
(CROWBAR THUDS)

107
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,216
(GRILLE CLATTERS)

108
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:39,858
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

109
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:43,153
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>You've reached the Rushville
Sheriff's Department.</i>

110
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:47,240
<i>If this is an emergency,
please hang up and dial 911.</i>

111
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,992
<i>Otherwise,
please leave a message</i>

112
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:50,785
<i>and someone
from the department...</i>

113
00:06:50,869 --> 00:06:52,829
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

114
00:06:57,626 --> 00:06:58,877
(KEYS JINGLING)

115
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:12,766
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

116
00:07:14,517 --> 00:07:17,562
(RING WARBLES)

117
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,444
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

118
00:07:25,403 --> 00:07:26,821
HAL: There you are.

119
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:29,032
- (RING PULSING)
- AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>This ring
will soon run out of charge.</i>

120
00:07:29,074 --> 00:07:30,200
- Fuck.
- AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Three,</i>

121
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,035
<i>two, one.</i>

122
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:36,539
- (EXHALES SHARPLY)
- (CAR DOOR CLOSES)

123
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:39,250
- (CAR ENGINE REVVING)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

124
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,089
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

125
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:48,259
(TIRES SCREECHING)

126
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:03,525
(KERRY KANE SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY ON MICROPHONE)

127
00:08:03,608 --> 00:08:07,612
- (CITIZEN SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)
- (OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

128
00:08:07,696 --> 00:08:09,781
(CHATTER STOPS)

129
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,449
- (DOOR HINGES CREAKING)
- ♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

130
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,953
Were you talking about me?

131
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:18,456
- (CHAIRS CREAKING)
- (FAINT MURMURS)

132
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:20,458
You were talking about me.

133
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:30,844
(SOFTLY) Excuse me.

134
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,638
Excuse me.

135
00:08:34,973 --> 00:08:36,016
Excuse me.

136
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:39,477
(CLEARS THROAT)

137
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:43,356
(FAINT MURMURS CONTINUE)

138
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:44,983
Carry on.

139
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:51,614
We were just talking
about whether to go ahead

140
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,491
with this Friday's
football game.

141
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,994
Would that be traumatizing,

142
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:59,122
or could it help
pull the community together?

143
00:08:59,164 --> 00:09:02,042
Coach,
you were about to say something.

144
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,172
Right. Yeah. Um...

145
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:09,716
I've been talking to the boys,

146
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:13,595
and, uh,
they're pretty shook up.

147
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:15,805
- This is also something
they've been working for...
- (QUIETLY) Hey.

148
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:17,640
- since two-a-days.
- (WHISPERS INDISTINCTLY)

149
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:19,225
COACH: Uh, I mean... (SIGHS)

150
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:21,561
- I guess I wonder what we're...
- BILL MACON: (WHISPERS)
Sorry. Sorry.

151
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:25,648
...what we're teaching 'em
if we just pack it up
and forfeit.

152
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:28,943
- KERRY: Yeah, I think that's
what we're trying to figure out.
- (QUIETLY) Good news.

153
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:31,488
- I got the judge
to drop your assault charges.
- (COACH RESUMES SPEAKING)

154
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,198
- Well, I appreciate that.
- (CHUCKLES)

155
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,242
- How much is it gonna cost me?
- Oh, no. It's on the house.

156
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:39,162
KERRY:
And, obviously, we're worried...

157
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,873
Good news is you're free
to go back to Coast City.

158
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,709
Or anywhere else you feel like
going for that matter.

159
00:09:44,793 --> 00:09:47,045
What was everyone talking about
when I came in here?

160
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,881
KERRY: ...well-placed,
to go ahead with the game
and playing.

161
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:52,008
Five people just died here.

162
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:54,761
An alien blew himself up
at the sheriff's station.

163
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:56,221
That's a lot to process.

164
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,347
Did your wife tell you

165
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:59,224
that alien was chirping
about vengeance

166
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:01,226
before he blew himself up?

167
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,397
Here's what I'd really like
to talk to you about.

168
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:09,025
I ended up
on that football field

169
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,527
because of a hunch. Hmm.

170
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,694
Just a gut feeling

171
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,404
that it was
gonna be extraterrestrial.

172
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:16,699
But your father's men,
they shot four people.

173
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:20,912
And yet, those guys' friend
ends up being an alien?

174
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:23,206
(COACH SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

175
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:24,874
Is that a... a question or...

176
00:10:24,958 --> 00:10:26,626
Uh, it's just a roundabout way
of saying

177
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:29,129
you don't shoot people
because of a gut feeling.

178
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:33,591
- I... I wouldn't know--
- HAL: No, I'm telling you.

179
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:35,635
- You don't.
- Okay.

180
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,888
So, how is it that father's men
knew who to target?

181
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,265
You'd have to ask him,
I don't--

182
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,516
HAL: I'm asking you
as my attorney,

183
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:43,059
someone who cares
about my wellbeing,

184
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:44,561
and apparently,
my travel schedule.

185
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:45,728
We are still talking

186
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,730
with attorney-client privilege,
I presume.

187
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,399
KERRY: Excuse me, honey?

188
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:50,608
BOTH: Yes?

189
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:53,820
KERRY: I was talking
to my husband.

190
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,280
Oh. Oh, yeah. Of course.

191
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:57,615
If you two
are gonna keep talking,

192
00:10:57,699 --> 00:10:59,534
I'm gonna need
Mr. Jordan to leave.

193
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,619
- He started it.
- Well...

194
00:11:01,703 --> 00:11:04,122
I've got about 30 seconds
of patience left.

195
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:05,623
I only need 40.

196
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:07,917
KERRY: And I'll be happy
to give them to you

197
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:09,294
when we're done here.

198
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:12,172
Well, how long
is that gonna take?

199
00:11:13,548 --> 00:11:16,467
- (MICROPHONE SCREECHING)
- It'll take as long as it takes.

200
00:11:16,551 --> 00:11:18,845
Yeah, I don't think
I can keep quiet that long.

201
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:21,264
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- (FAINT CHATTER)

202
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:24,934
Oh, uh, sorry,
I gotta... I gotta take this.

203
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:27,395
Yeah. As you were.

204
00:11:28,897 --> 00:11:29,981
Talk to me, Junior.

205
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,150
- JOHN: This house is insane.
- (BIRD CHIRPING)

206
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,651
HAL: <i>That's what you called
to tell me?</i>

207
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,945
JOHN: No, no,
I can't find the key.

208
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:38,031
HAL: Well, did you look
under the rock?

209
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:41,451
Which rock, Hal?

210
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:43,328
HAL: <i>To the left
of the door under the bush.</i>

211
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:44,621
(GRUNTS)

212
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,497
- It looks like a potato
with a smile.
- (CAR ENGINE STARTING)

213
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:49,000
HAL: Or a frown
if I left it upside down.

214
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,501
Potato rock.

215
00:11:50,585 --> 00:11:53,213
♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

216
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:01,304
(KEY CLATTERS)

217
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:05,808
(CHIRPS)

218
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,101
So, how's it going over there?

219
00:12:08,311 --> 00:12:10,605
I get the feeling
everyone wants me gone.

220
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:16,527
Kinda makes me feel
like I need to stick around.

221
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:18,154
It would make you think that.

222
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:19,864
HAL: <i>The lantern's in my closet.</i>

223
00:12:19,948 --> 00:12:22,450
<i>If you're at the front door,
it's upstairs to the left.</i>

224
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:28,289
So, how much
do Lanterns get paid anyway?

225
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:29,374
Not enough.

226
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,834
I can tell you that.

227
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:35,129
- JOHN: <i>Well,
your house begs to differ.</i>
- (DOOR RATTLING)

228
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,006
(GLASS CLATTERING)

229
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:39,008
- JOHN: <i>What the hell was that?</i>
- Don't worry about it.

230
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:43,513
<i>I got the house from a rich guy.
Saved his kid.</i>

231
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:45,848
<i>His dad felt like shit
because he couldn't help.</i>

232
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:49,394
I didn't want to emasculate him
anymore, so I...

233
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,857
let him buy me a house.

234
00:12:55,942 --> 00:12:58,319
So, when are you actually going
to move into this place?

235
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:00,697
What are you talking about?

236
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:03,032
I've lived in that house
for eight years.

237
00:13:03,074 --> 00:13:06,035
- JOHN: <i>You've got no furniture.</i>
- (GRUNTS) I have a bed.

238
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:07,495
