346
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:59,365
- (ECHOING THUD)
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

347
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:05,996
(POLICE SIREN WAILING)

348
00:20:10,376 --> 00:20:12,545
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

349
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:15,423
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

350
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:25,558
(CAR ENGINE RUNNING)

351
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,322
Is this about me
not being on the insurance?

352
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:42,533
(SNIFFS)

353
00:20:42,616 --> 00:20:44,410
It is pretty much
exactly what it looks like.

354
00:20:44,493 --> 00:20:45,661
But in my defense,

355
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,663
I wanted to talk to you
about this at the meeting,

356
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:48,789
and you shushed me.

357
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:53,002
You're killing me, Jordan.
You know that?

358
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:56,005
Just a slow, painful death.

359
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:58,591
There's more going on here
than you realize.

360
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:01,010
You mean like you going
to the stadium

361
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:03,846
and dragging these corpses
through the metal detector,

362
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:07,475
which you now realize
is actually an alien detector?

363
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,019
Uh, let me rephrase.

364
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:13,355
You obviously realize
exactly what's going on here.

365
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:16,484
Congratulations.
You've caught up to me.

366
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:19,195
Now, would you just please
let me do my job?

367
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:21,530
Is this a good time
to talk about jurisdiction?

368
00:21:21,614 --> 00:21:22,698
Because you seemed
really hung up

369
00:21:22,782 --> 00:21:24,074
on what was terrestrial
and what wasn't.

370
00:21:24,158 --> 00:21:26,452
- And as far as--
- Where are you going
with these guys?

371
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,828
To visit your father-in-law.

372
00:21:30,581 --> 00:21:34,835
May I just say,
that is a profoundly bad idea.

373
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:37,338
Did he put up those detectors?

374
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:39,256
- He did.
- Do you know where he got them?

375
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,091
- I do not.
- You're not even curious?

376
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:43,928
It's not against the law
to be obsessed with aliens.

377
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:45,513
Trust me, I wish it was.

378
00:21:45,596 --> 00:21:47,890
It'd make my marriage
a hell of a lot smoother.

379
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:49,099
Your marriage is unsmooth?

380
00:21:49,183 --> 00:21:53,020
The fact is, Macon hasn't done
anything illegal.

381
00:21:53,062 --> 00:21:55,731
Now, he was cordial
when he needed you,

382
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:57,191
but if you show up today

383
00:21:57,233 --> 00:22:00,444
with all your questions
and all your attitude,

384
00:22:00,528 --> 00:22:02,321
it is not gonna go well.

385
00:22:03,531 --> 00:22:04,615
Whose side are you on?

386
00:22:07,368 --> 00:22:10,204
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
- (SNIFFS, EXHALES SHARPLY)

387
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,670
I'll take you,
but you let me do the talking.

388
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:20,464
Understood?

389
00:22:20,548 --> 00:22:22,967
- Well, I don't know if I--
- Just nod.

390
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:26,804
KERRY: Follow me.

391
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,223
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

392
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:40,818
Hey, Ben.

393
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,528
I'd like to see
your boss, please.

394
00:22:44,405 --> 00:22:47,116
I'm afraid
he's not accepting visitors.

395
00:22:47,157 --> 00:22:49,577
Yeah, I get that. Absolutely.

396
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:51,495
You know, sometimes
you just gotta accept things

397
00:22:51,579 --> 00:22:53,205
that take you
out of your comfort zone.

398
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:56,000
Is he speaking for you?

399
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:58,794
Right now,
he's pretty much just speaking.

400
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:01,422
This is part of
an official investigation, son.

401
00:23:02,715 --> 00:23:05,259
- Is that true?
- Evidently.

402
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:07,177
Well, in that case,
can I see your warrant?

403
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:12,600
Well, look at that. The cavalry.
Just in the nick of time.

404
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:17,521
(HORSE NEIGHS)

405
00:23:20,024 --> 00:23:22,610
The calvary's a lot faster
in the movies.

406
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,778
I told them
you aren't seeing any visitors.

407
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:28,032
That's okay, Ben. Hey, Kerry.

408
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:31,160
You know I'm a fan of your work.

409
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:33,787
But I confess, I'm confused
as to why you're still in town.

410
00:23:34,455 --> 00:23:35,706
Four aliens are dead.

411
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:37,541
Their accomplice
blew himself up.

412
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:39,585
And yet, you linger.

413
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:41,587
Well, that's what
your son told me.

414
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:44,298
But, uh...
Well, here's what I think.

415
00:23:45,925 --> 00:23:47,509
I think you're hiding something
on this property

416
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,552
you don't want me to see.

417
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:50,471
I had you as a guest here
just the other day.

418
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:51,805
Because you wanted me to prove

419
00:23:51,889 --> 00:23:53,849
that that fella
in custody was an alien.

420
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:56,143
Which you did. Like I said,
I'm a fan of your work,

421
00:23:56,226 --> 00:23:57,978
- but your work here's done.
- Oh, I just need a minute

422
00:23:58,062 --> 00:23:59,521
- of your time.
- I believe you've had it.

423
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:01,690
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

424
00:24:01,774 --> 00:24:03,776
Front gate, eleven o'clock.

425
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:06,362
(RADIO BEEPING)

426
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:08,364
Oh, boy.
Am I about to be threatened?

427
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:10,699
I got four dead bodies in my car

428
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:12,576
that set off
the hidden camera and alarm

429
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:14,370
when I drag 'em
through those metal detectors

430
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:16,664
you got set up
at the stadium there.

431
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:20,042
Now, I don't want to disparage
your small, little town,

432
00:24:20,084 --> 00:24:21,377
but I've been
all over the galaxy,

433
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:23,045
and I don't think
I've ever seen technology

434
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,296
quite that sophisticated.

435
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:26,840
I told you.

436
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:30,886
People who walked this land
before me,

437
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:32,888
they got caught flat-footed
when the settlers come in

438
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,598
and colonized 'em.

439
00:24:34,682 --> 00:24:36,558
I'm not about to make
that same mistake again.

440
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:38,560
And how about that technology?

441
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:40,771
Very generous gift from the man
who funds this property.

442
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:42,356
- Oh, your benefactor?
- WILL MACON: Correct.

443
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:43,774
Tell me the truth.
Is he even real,

444
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:45,442
or is this some
Keyser Söze situation?

445
00:24:45,526 --> 00:24:46,819
Oh, I assure you,
he's very real.

446
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:47,987
HAL:
Then what's his name again?

447
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,238
I'm not at liberty to say.

448
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:50,948
- Because of the NDA.
- WILL: That's right.

449
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:52,074
That's-- You know,

450
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,118
- do all cowboys have NDAs...
- That's it.

451
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:55,828
- We're leaving.
- ...or are you just
a special cowboy?

452
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:56,912
No, I'm serious.

453
00:24:56,996 --> 00:25:00,082
You got this whole Marlboro Man
thing happening here,

454
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:02,584
but yet you can't be straight
with me because of an NDA?

455
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,253
Hell, even that other guy,

456
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:05,921
he was selling cigarettes
to kids,

457
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:07,798
and he still didn't let
those lawyers stop him

458
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:09,717
from saying
whatever the hell he wanted.

459
00:25:13,303 --> 00:25:15,180
I want to know
what other technology you got

460
00:25:15,264 --> 00:25:16,598
in this compound.

461
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,767
I think
it's important for you to know

462
00:25:18,809 --> 00:25:20,477
there's a man with a rifle
in that guard tower

463
00:25:20,561 --> 00:25:21,937
with instructions
to shoot anybody

464
00:25:22,021 --> 00:25:23,272
who trespasses on this property.

465
00:25:24,648 --> 00:25:26,150
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

466
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,485
Well, you can't do that.

467
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:34,575
- Can he do that?
- He can absolutely do that.

468
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:36,160
Well, that just seems
unneighborly.

469
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:37,828
Sheriff.

470
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:39,663
HAL: I'm coming on.

471
00:25:39,747 --> 00:25:41,457
You're gonna have to deal
with me.

472
00:25:42,332 --> 00:25:44,251
Oh, for Christ's sake,
I got the ring.

473
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:46,420
You try to shoot me,
and I'm just gonna put up--

474
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:47,713
♪ (MUSIC STOPS ABRUPTLY) ♪

475
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:51,008
- (CHAIR RATTLING)
- (JOHN BREATHING HEAVILY)

476
00:25:57,097 --> 00:25:59,099
I apologize for the violence.

477
00:26:00,976 --> 00:26:03,145
- (BIRD CHIRPING)
- Yeah.

478
00:26:03,187 --> 00:26:06,815
May I ask you a question
about the bird, John Stewart?

479
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:08,817
Sure.

480
00:26:08,859 --> 00:26:10,486
It's a wildly
impressive construct,

481
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,154
but how does
Hal Jordan continue

482
00:26:12,196 --> 00:26:14,239
to project it
from such a great distance?

483
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,910
He's not projecting it. I am.

484
00:26:18,869 --> 00:26:19,995
You're not wearing a ring.

485
00:26:20,037 --> 00:26:22,122
Did you tie me up
to ask me questions

486
00:26:22,206 --> 00:26:23,290
about my fucking bird?

487
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:26,085
No, I tied you up
to ask you about Manhunters.

488
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,175
I'm sorry.
Was I supposed to react?

489
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,343
Yeah, you are.

490
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:36,512
Because you think
I know what a Manhunter is?

491
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,971
ANTAAN: Given your proximity
to Hal Jordan,

492
00:26:38,055 --> 00:26:39,598
it'd be very hard
to believe that you do not.

493
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:41,308
Proximity. You mean "closeness"?

494
00:26:41,350 --> 00:26:44,186
That's a better word, yes.
That's a much better word.

495
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:47,022
JOHN: I see human
isn't your first language here.

496
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:51,026
I'm not even close
to close with Hal Jordan.

497
00:26:51,068 --> 00:26:53,570
In fact, he sent me here
to get rid of me,

498
00:26:53,654 --> 00:26:54,905
so I'm sorry, gentlemen.

499
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,198
♪ (FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

500
00:26:56,281 --> 00:26:57,741
But you're about to torture
a man

501
00:26:57,825 --> 00:26:59,118
who doesn't know shit.

502
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:05,541
(LAUGHS)

503
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:07,000
Torture? No, John.

504
00:27:07,835 --> 00:27:09,169
We don't want
to torture you, John.

505
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,088
We want to recruit you.

506
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,676
You don't tell someone
when you wanna recruit them.

507
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:18,554
You have to be more subtle.

508
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:20,222
ANTAAN: We don't have time
for subtlety, John.

509
00:27:20,264 --> 00:27:22,516
One of the most dangerous beings
to ever exist

510
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:24,560
knows it has been found,
which means right now

511
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:26,103
it is preparing
its brutal response.

512
00:27:27,104 --> 00:27:28,397
And that's a Manhunter?

513
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:30,232
You think the Green Lanterns
came first?

514
00:27:30,274 --> 00:27:32,401
- You really don't know?
- I really don't know.

515
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:33,986
Well, that makes things
much easier.

516
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:35,320
I don't have to change
your mind.

517
00:27:35,404 --> 00:27:36,655
I just need to stamp it.

518
00:27:36,738 --> 00:27:38,157
What the fuck
do you mean, stamp?

519
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:43,871
Imprint? Um...

520
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:46,623
- Enlighten.
- I don't need enlightenment.

521
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:51,086
There was a time of chaos
in the galaxy.

522
00:27:51,128 --> 00:27:53,797
- Then the Manhunters came.
- (MECHANISM CLICKING)

523
00:27:53,881 --> 00:27:55,257
ANTAAN: We don't know
where they came from,

524
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,633
just that they were synthetic.

525
00:27:57,634 --> 00:27:58,927
And able to build new bodies,

526
00:27:58,969 --> 00:28:00,929
which meant they could take
the form of any species

527
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:04,224
and embed, undetected,
within any society.

528
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:06,602
This ability to build
allowed them

529
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:08,020
to invent technologies

530
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:10,898
far beyond the limits
of the planets they inhabited.

531
00:28:10,981 --> 00:28:14,067
They were brutal.
They were deceptive.

532
00:28:14,151 --> 00:28:16,904
They carried out
what they called "justice."

533
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,740
Entire species were lost.

534
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:20,782
(DEVICE CLICKS, HUMS)

535
00:28:20,866 --> 00:28:22,618
ANTAAN: And then,
as mysteriously as they arrived,

536
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:23,785
they were gone.

537
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:25,829
At least
we thought they were gone.

538
00:28:25,913 --> 00:28:28,582
In reality, one of them remained
on our planet,

539
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:29,625
passing as one of us

540
00:28:29,666 --> 00:28:31,793
while he quietly engineered
a holocaust.

541
00:28:33,295 --> 00:28:35,088
Have you ever been deceived
by someone you love?

542
00:28:36,506 --> 00:28:37,633
Yeah.

543
00:28:37,716 --> 00:28:39,801
Then you'll understand
when you experience

544
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,429
what he did to us.

545
00:28:45,349 --> 00:28:47,976
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

546
00:28:48,018 --> 00:28:49,269
(CHIRPING)

547
00:28:51,772 --> 00:28:54,399
Get off. (GRUNTS)

548
00:28:55,651 --> 00:28:58,278
I'm sorry, but you need to see.

549
00:28:58,362 --> 00:29:01,198
- (DEVICE BUZZING)
- (GROANS)

550
00:29:01,281 --> 00:29:03,283
- ♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
- (SCREAMS)

551
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:04,826
ANTAAN: This is what
it looks like

552
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:07,204
when a Manhunter
destroys your people.

553
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:10,749
John, do you see
what it feels like?

554
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:12,084
(JOHN SOBS)

555
00:29:12,167 --> 00:29:14,461
- ANTAAN: See it!
- (GROANS)

556
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:16,672
ANTAAN: Do you see
what it did to them, John?

557
00:29:16,713 --> 00:29:19,925
- Do you see it?
- (SCREAMS)

558
00:29:20,008 --> 00:29:21,051
ANTAAN: See it!

559
00:29:22,219 --> 00:29:24,805
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

560
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:26,348
- (DEVICE TURNS OFF)
- ♪ (MUSIC FALLS) ♪

561
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:27,516
(PANTS)

562
00:29:30,394 --> 00:29:32,896
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

563
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:38,318
(GRUNTS)

564
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:44,908
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

565
00:29:44,992 --> 00:29:46,868
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

566
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:48,662
The effects
of our collective loss

567
00:29:48,745 --> 00:29:50,455
will remain with you
for some time.

568
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,791
I'm sorry.

569
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:00,007
The scale of our tragedy
drew the attention

570
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:02,134
of a Green Lantern
sent by the Guardians.

571
00:30:03,218 --> 00:30:05,137
The Lantern

572
00:30:06,263 --> 00:30:07,889
took the monster
into his custody

573
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:09,683
and guaranteed
he'd be executed.

574
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:14,313
- Why?
- ANTAAN: I do not know.

575
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:16,398
It does not matter,

576
00:30:16,481 --> 00:30:18,567
but we believed, somewhere,
the Manhunter was still alive.

577
00:30:20,027 --> 00:30:24,489
So, we searched, John.
We searched for years.

578
00:30:24,573 --> 00:30:26,658
Until finally we discovered
where he was hiding.

579
00:30:28,535 --> 00:30:29,578
Rushville.

580
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,580
ANTAAN:
Our detection is limited.

581
00:30:31,621 --> 00:30:33,707
There's radiation unique
to the Manhunter,

582
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:35,584
though he could be disguised
as any human.

583
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:37,711
To find out which,
we had to get close.

584
00:30:38,628 --> 00:30:40,756
But our team was exposed
and killed.

585
00:30:43,467 --> 00:30:44,926
And who should arrive
an hour later?

586
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:46,636
Jordan.

587
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:49,598
You think he was trying
to protect the thing?

588
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:50,849
ANTAAN: Perhaps.

589
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:53,101
Our target knows
we've located him.

590
00:30:53,143 --> 00:30:55,562
And we cannot enter Rushville
without being detected.

591
00:30:55,645 --> 00:30:58,482
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

592
00:30:58,565 --> 00:30:59,608
So, you...

593
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:02,986
you must identify the Manhunter.

594
00:31:05,822 --> 00:31:07,616
How the fuck
am I supposed to do that?

595
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:08,742
Your bird.

596
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:10,911
This bird is proof
you can achieve the impossible.

597
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:14,289
Now, we could fulfill
our mission

598
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:16,958
by walking into the town square
and detonating ourselves,

599
00:31:17,042 --> 00:31:18,919
but that would destroy
Rushville.

600
00:31:20,462 --> 00:31:23,131
No reason for innocent lives
to be lost.

601
00:31:23,215 --> 00:31:26,259
Because it took a human form,
it could be killed as a human.

602
00:31:26,927 --> 00:31:28,887
You have 48 hours, John.

603
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:32,349
Find the Manhunter.

604
00:31:36,395 --> 00:31:37,437
Once you do...

605
00:31:39,356 --> 00:31:40,982
contact us.

606
00:31:41,066 --> 00:31:43,026
- If you fail to contact us--
- Yeah, I got it.

607
00:31:46,655 --> 00:31:48,240
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

608
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:51,118
- (INHALES SHARPLY)
- (MONITOR BEEPING)

609
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:58,708
KERRY: Hey, there.

610
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:03,422
They shot me.

611
00:32:05,215 --> 00:32:07,175
KERRY: You were trespassing.

612
00:32:07,259 --> 00:32:08,885
Might as well have walked
onto that ranch

613
00:32:08,969 --> 00:32:10,720
with a sign
that said, "Shoot me."

614
00:32:12,389 --> 00:32:15,308
- How are you feeling?
- Uh, all right.

615
00:32:15,392 --> 00:32:17,769
A little sore.
How long have I been out?

616
00:32:18,854 --> 00:32:21,606
Not too long.
They cleared you to go.

617
00:32:21,690 --> 00:32:23,817
Just wanted you
to sleep off the anesthesia.

618
00:32:24,985 --> 00:32:28,238
(PANTS)

619
00:32:32,159 --> 00:32:33,201
So...

620
00:32:34,327 --> 00:32:36,455
what's with Sinestro?

621
00:32:37,998 --> 00:32:39,458
Why are you asking me that?

622
00:32:40,750 --> 00:32:43,003
KERRY: You kept saying his name
in your sleep.

623
00:32:45,172 --> 00:32:46,840
I'm not authorized
to talk about that.

624
00:32:48,508 --> 00:32:50,927
It's not exactly top secret.

625
00:32:53,013 --> 00:32:57,434
It says here, "He was a Lantern,
attempted a coup,

626
00:32:57,517 --> 00:32:59,603
killed one of the bosses."

627
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:03,773
It also says you were the one
who took him down.

628
00:33:08,069 --> 00:33:09,821
I don't talk about that.

629
00:33:09,905 --> 00:33:13,158
Except that you do,
in your sleep.

630
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,368
- How...
- (HANDCUFF RATTLES)

631
00:33:18,371 --> 00:33:20,081
You gotta be kidding me.

632
00:33:20,165 --> 00:33:22,751
Like I said,
you were trespassing.

633
00:33:22,834 --> 00:33:24,169
HAL: In the name of Tom Osborne,

634
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,921
or whoever it is
that you worship,

635
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,881
please take these off.

636
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:32,093
Not until you listen to me.
Can you manage that?

637
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:34,971
- Yes, ma'am.
- Good.

638
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:37,933
Because every time
you don't listen,

639
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:39,351
or you steal bodies,

640
00:33:39,434 --> 00:33:42,103
or storm
my father-in-law's compound

641
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:45,607
and don't let me do the talking,
what you're really doing

642
00:33:45,649 --> 00:33:47,859
is cutting my legs
straight out from under me.

643
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:50,904
I'm the sheriff.

644
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:54,157
If you don't follow my lead,
you're legitimizing this idea

645
00:33:54,241 --> 00:33:57,244
that Macon is the seat of power.
And trust me,

646
00:33:58,245 --> 00:34:00,914
you do not want to help
push that narrative.

647
00:34:02,666 --> 00:34:04,209
This is my town.

648
00:34:04,292 --> 00:34:06,962
I have worked my ass off
to earn people's respect,

649
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:09,089
and I can't have you
undermining that.

650
00:34:12,509 --> 00:34:13,593
You're right.

651
00:34:16,346 --> 00:34:18,348
I'm sorry. You're right.

652
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:25,063
So, you're gonna go back
to your motel

653
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:26,439
and let me do my job?

654
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:29,776
No more storming the compound?

655
00:34:31,444 --> 00:34:33,613
I swear on Tom Osborne's life.

656
00:34:49,588 --> 00:34:51,006
(HANDCUFF UNLOCKS)

657
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:53,675
And for the record,
I'm not on your side.

658
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:56,177
I'm not on Macon's side.
I'm on my side,

659
00:34:57,053 --> 00:34:58,888
trying to hold
this town together.

660
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:04,561
(SIGHS)

661
00:35:07,564 --> 00:35:09,649
Can I ask you a question?

662
00:35:09,733 --> 00:35:11,901
If I knew
about the alien detectors,

663
00:35:11,985 --> 00:35:13,903
why did I fight you
on jurisdiction?

664
00:35:14,904 --> 00:35:16,239
Does make a guy wonder.

665
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:21,036
The others were dead.

666
00:35:21,077 --> 00:35:23,455
I assumed if Waylon
didn't set off the alarm,

667
00:35:23,538 --> 00:35:24,789
he wasn't an alien.

668
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:26,916
I was wrong.

669
00:35:27,959 --> 00:35:29,002
It happens.

670
00:35:30,045 --> 00:35:31,838
KERRY: It shouldn't. Look.

671
00:35:32,881 --> 00:35:35,634
I apologize
for trying to obstruct you.

672
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:39,137
I just didn't want Billy's dad

673
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:41,056
insurrecting the shit
out of everyone

674
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:44,434
and getting them all paranoid
about invasion.

675
00:35:45,644 --> 00:35:47,103
So much for that plan.

676
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:51,941
Thanks for being straight
with me.

677
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:57,030
Thanks for not dying
in my jurisdiction.

678
00:35:57,113 --> 00:35:58,114
(CHUCKLES DRYLY)

679
00:36:00,617 --> 00:36:02,118
KERRY: My turn for a question.

680
00:36:03,787 --> 00:36:06,122
Why am I still in town
if the threat's over?

681
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:08,792
It does make a girl wonder.

682
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:11,961
Something is off here.
I can feel it.

683
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,592
Why do you want me gone?

684
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:21,471
Everything feels
like it's about to explode

685
00:36:21,554 --> 00:36:23,014
for no good reason.

686
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:26,017
This place is losing its mind.

687
00:36:27,227 --> 00:36:30,313
You kicking up dust
and getting shot isn't helping.

688
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:35,068
If I need you, I can call.

689
00:36:40,323 --> 00:36:41,741
You were at my bedside.

690
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:45,620
It's a great book.

691
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:48,248
It's hard to find time
to read with a kid at home.

692
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:54,671
- (TELEPHONE RINGING)
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

693
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:10,061
(SIGHS) So,
where are you from, anyway?

694
00:37:11,521 --> 00:37:13,398
You decide
to actually make nice,

695
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:16,151
and that's the best you got?
"Where you from?"

696
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:18,278
Well, you don't exactly
scream Rushville.

697
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:21,406
- (SCOFFS) You're a snob.
- Doesn't mean I'm wrong.

698
00:37:22,699 --> 00:37:26,202
I'm from Gotham.
Moved here on a whim.

699
00:37:26,286 --> 00:37:28,872
- That sounds like a story.
- Doesn't it?

700
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:33,334
- That's all I'm gonna get?
- Pretty much.

701
00:37:33,918 --> 00:37:36,171
Hmm. I'll take it for now.

702
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:38,548
KERRY:
Because you're not leaving.

703
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:40,800
You didn't hear a word I said
in there, did you?

704
00:37:40,884 --> 00:37:43,803
Well, I heard a few of 'em.
Where are all the patients?

705
00:37:43,845 --> 00:37:46,723
It's a small town,
not exactly a big patient pool.

706
00:37:46,806 --> 00:37:48,516
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

707
00:37:48,558 --> 00:37:49,976
(SIGHS)

708
00:37:50,059 --> 00:37:51,060
Half the equipment looks

709
00:37:51,144 --> 00:37:52,854
like it was just taken out
of the crate.

710
00:37:52,896 --> 00:37:54,439
Yeah, well,
mostly everyone's smart enough

711
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:56,024
not to get themselves shot.

712
00:37:57,525 --> 00:38:00,111
- (THUNDER RUMBLES)
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

713
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:09,245
JOHN: Thank you.
Just over here is great.

714
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:16,669
There you go. Thank you.

715
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:20,548
- (BELL RINGING)
- (BIRD CHIRPS)

716
00:38:20,632 --> 00:38:23,218
♪ (SOFT COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS) ♪

717
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:25,303
(FAINT CHATTER)

718
00:38:25,386 --> 00:38:26,429
(DOOR CLOSES)

719
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:31,684
- (DOOR OPENS)
- (BELL RINGING)

720
00:38:31,768 --> 00:38:33,102
(GROANS) Hey.

721
00:38:33,937 --> 00:38:36,064
- Um, can I get a...
- (DOOR CLOSES)

722
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:38,024
I... I'll get a decaf, please.
Thank you.

723
00:38:38,066 --> 00:38:40,109
- SERVER: Of course.
- (BIRD TWEETS)

724
00:38:40,193 --> 00:38:41,569
(COOKWARE CLANKING)

725
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:44,113
- (JOHN SIGHS)
- (DOOR HINGES CREAKING)

726
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:54,457
It's a small town,
bound to happen.

727
00:38:57,043 --> 00:38:57,961
Yeah.

728
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:00,296
ZOE MACON: The booths
are more comfortable.

729
00:39:01,631 --> 00:39:03,591
Uh, it's been a long day.

730
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:06,636
I'm just trying to clear my head
for a second.

731
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:08,471
Yeah, yeah. Fair enough.

732
00:39:08,555 --> 00:39:11,307
- (COFFEE POURING)
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)

733
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:15,979
Thank you very much.

734
00:39:16,062 --> 00:39:17,313
- Here you go.
- JOHN: Thanks.

735
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:22,151
(BIRD TWEETING)

736
00:39:42,839 --> 00:39:44,048
(SIGHS)

737
00:39:45,508 --> 00:39:48,011
Um, for the record,

738
00:39:49,429 --> 00:39:51,764
I wouldn't have slept with you
if I knew you were married.

739
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:57,020
Well, I'm glad you didn't know.

740
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:01,149
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

741
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:02,650
You into that kind of thing?

742
00:40:04,027 --> 00:40:05,486
ZOE: What kind of thing is that?

743
00:40:07,447 --> 00:40:08,823
I mean, uh...

744
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:12,035
is your relationship
unconventional?

745
00:40:16,039 --> 00:40:17,206
You've met my husband, right?

746
00:40:17,290 --> 00:40:18,291
- JOHN: Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

747
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:19,834
Yeah. What do you think?

748
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:22,545
Uh, respectfully? I think
he's pretty fucking weird.

749
00:40:22,629 --> 00:40:25,214
(LAUGHS) Yeah, that he is.
Deeply so.

750
00:40:25,298 --> 00:40:26,966
Yeah. I think
he's pretty fucking weird,

751
00:40:27,050 --> 00:40:28,051
but you're not.

752
00:40:29,552 --> 00:40:30,553
(CUP CLINKS)

753
00:40:31,596 --> 00:40:35,516
- How can you be so sure?
- Uh, I see you. Um...

754
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:37,393
I don't think
you would do anything

755
00:40:37,477 --> 00:40:40,021
without thinking about it first.
You know?

756
00:40:40,063 --> 00:40:43,858
White men have the privilege
of being eccentric.

757
00:40:45,068 --> 00:40:47,028
White men with money?

758
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:49,697
They can do
whatever the fuck they want.

759
00:40:50,365 --> 00:40:53,284
Play cowboy, build castles.

760
00:40:53,368 --> 00:40:56,746
- Do you like that?
- ZOE: Yeah. I like the security.

761
00:40:56,829 --> 00:40:58,247
I also like
that he could've bought

762
00:40:58,331 --> 00:41:00,291
some blonde bimbo from Texas
to be his arm candy,

763
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:01,501
but he wanted me.

764
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:04,629
I'm sure a lot
of people want you.

765
00:41:04,712 --> 00:41:05,713
ZOE: None...

766
00:41:07,423 --> 00:41:08,967
that could give me what he has.

767
00:41:10,510 --> 00:41:11,552
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

768
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:13,304
It's a lot to deal with,
I know, but...

769
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:15,682
but it's worth it, I think.

770
00:41:16,766 --> 00:41:19,560
And when I need a break,
I just take one.

771
00:41:19,644 --> 00:41:22,063
So, you'll put up with some
deeply weird White man

772
00:41:22,105 --> 00:41:24,273
with a savior complex
just to live the life?

773
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:26,776
No, I'm with my husband
because I love him.

774
00:41:27,944 --> 00:41:29,445
And I know he loves me.

775
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,118
Hey, how's your White man?

776
00:41:35,201 --> 00:41:36,369
(CHUCKLES)

777
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:39,330
Uh, how is he?

778
00:41:40,873 --> 00:41:42,125
He wanted me out the way,

779
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:44,752
so he, uh... he sent me
to fetch his things.

780
00:41:50,383 --> 00:41:53,302
Is that why you were trying
to clear your head over there?

781
00:41:57,765 --> 00:41:58,808
Uh...

782
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:03,396
I'm just trying to figure out
if I can trust him.

783
00:42:03,479 --> 00:42:05,690
ZOE: If you have to ask
the question,

784
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:08,234
then you already know
the answer.

785
00:42:11,988 --> 00:42:14,073
(CAR ENGINE RUMBLING)

786
00:42:22,248 --> 00:42:25,001
(BIRD CHIRPING)

787
00:42:34,177 --> 00:42:36,929
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

788
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:39,182
JOHN: Nope.

789
00:42:40,933 --> 00:42:42,143
Don't.

790
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,191
What happened to you?

791
00:42:48,900 --> 00:42:50,151
Your girlfriend's husband

792
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:52,153
sicced one of you sniper-types
on me.

793
00:42:52,195 --> 00:42:54,655
- Oh. Shoulder?
- HAL: Mm-hmm.

794
00:42:55,573 --> 00:42:57,325
Through and through?

795
00:42:57,366 --> 00:42:59,410
Yeah, it's a nice warning shot.

796
00:42:59,494 --> 00:43:01,162
Good to know
you're a fan of his work.

797
00:43:01,204 --> 00:43:03,456
- Yeah.
- (HAL GRUNTS)

798
00:43:05,208 --> 00:43:08,711
- (DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)
- (ZIPPER OPENS)

799
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:15,551
I told you
not to bring the suit.

800
00:43:16,511 --> 00:43:18,387
Yeah, well,
maybe I couldn't bring myself

801
00:43:18,471 --> 00:43:19,847
to just disrespect it.

802
00:43:19,931 --> 00:43:21,557
What else were you doing
while you were rummaging

803
00:43:21,641 --> 00:43:22,892
through my stuff?

804
00:43:22,975 --> 00:43:25,770
Dance around in my bathrobes?
Sing into my hairbrush?

805
00:43:28,106 --> 00:43:29,065
(LANTERN WHIRRING)

806
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:30,733
HAL: "In brightest day,
in blackest night,

807
00:43:30,817 --> 00:43:31,943
no evil shall escape my sight.

808
00:43:32,026 --> 00:43:33,361
Let those who worship
evil's might

809
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:35,113
beware my power,
Green Lantern's light."

810
00:43:35,196 --> 00:43:37,198
- (WHIRRING STOPS)
- (SIGHS)

811
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:39,075
There's something
on that compound.

812
00:43:39,867 --> 00:43:41,202
Benefactor's the key.

813
00:43:41,244 --> 00:43:43,579
We're not leaving here
until we find out who he is

814
00:43:43,663 --> 00:43:44,872
and what they're hiding.

815
00:43:44,914 --> 00:43:46,541
Yeah.

816
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:49,627
- Whatever you say.
- (BIRD CHIRPING)

817
00:43:52,255 --> 00:43:54,298
HAL: Hey, you might want to, uh,

818
00:43:54,382 --> 00:43:56,801
check the fine print
on that insurance policy.

819
00:44:11,482 --> 00:44:13,568
What the hell's
all over the seats?

820
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:16,946
I believe, uh, technically
they call that alien goo.

821
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:19,365
(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

822
00:44:22,618 --> 00:44:23,661
(CAR DOOR SLAMS SHUT)

823
00:44:25,913 --> 00:44:26,831
(CHUCKLES)

824
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:29,458
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

825
00:44:39,969 --> 00:44:41,637
What do you know
about Manhunters?

826
00:44:45,141 --> 00:44:46,309
Where'd you hear that word?

827
00:44:46,392 --> 00:44:49,562
Our buddy Waylon had friends.
They followed me onto the plane,

828
00:44:49,645 --> 00:44:51,564
snatched me outside
of your house.

829
00:44:51,647 --> 00:44:52,940
They're convinced
there's a Manhunter

830
00:44:53,024 --> 00:44:54,108
here in Rushville.

831
00:44:55,151 --> 00:44:56,319
(HAL GRUNTS)

832
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:03,075
So, what did they want with you?

833
00:45:03,159 --> 00:45:07,622
They want me to ID him.
And give him a call in 48 hours.

834
00:45:07,705 --> 00:45:10,458
Otherwise, they'll blow up
half of western Nebraska.

835
00:45:10,541 --> 00:45:11,667
Why you?

836
00:45:11,751 --> 00:45:14,879
Because they don't trust you.
In fact, he made it explicit

837
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:16,714
that I shouldn't tell you
any of this.

838
00:45:16,797 --> 00:45:18,633
- What else?
- JOHN: Just that he thinks

839
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:21,135
the Guardians
may have hid the Manhunter here.

840
00:45:21,219 --> 00:45:23,971
- They wouldn't do that.
- Well, shit. That's what I said.

841
00:45:24,013 --> 00:45:26,140
I knew there was something
about this place.

842
00:45:26,224 --> 00:45:28,267
And my gut is never wrong.

843
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,521
(BIRD CHIRPING)

844
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:38,152
Abin Sur must have brought
him here

845
00:45:38,236 --> 00:45:39,612
and the Manhunter killed him.

846
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:42,281
Yeah, and then you got
your ring.

847
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,618
What else can you tell me
about Manhunters?

848
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:47,078
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

849
00:45:47,161 --> 00:45:48,537
It's above
your pay grade, Junior.

850
00:45:48,621 --> 00:45:51,666
JOHN: No, it's not.
I told you he was here.

851
00:45:51,749 --> 00:45:54,335
Oh, so now Mr. Chain of Command
wants me to break the rules?

852
00:45:54,418 --> 00:45:56,170
Hal, they don't know
what form he's taken.

853
00:45:56,212 --> 00:45:58,714
He could be anyone in town.

854
00:46:00,007 --> 00:46:01,634
♪ (MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

855
00:46:02,301 --> 00:46:03,594
What else did they say to you?

856
00:46:06,722 --> 00:46:08,224
You know, just that, um,

857
00:46:09,392 --> 00:46:10,977
to create a living thing,

858
00:46:12,144 --> 00:46:15,356
let alone keeping it alive
while not wearing the ring,

859
00:46:15,398 --> 00:46:16,857
is so advanced

860
00:46:16,899 --> 00:46:18,484
that it's practically
impossible.

861
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:20,945
But I figured
that couldn't be true,

862
00:46:21,028 --> 00:46:22,989
'cause if it was,

863
00:46:23,030 --> 00:46:25,116
you would've at least given me
a hoorah.

864
00:46:27,159 --> 00:46:28,411
Hoorah.

865
00:46:34,834 --> 00:46:36,085
Forty-eight hours, huh?

866
00:46:37,878 --> 00:46:39,463
Yeah, 48.

867
00:46:39,547 --> 00:46:41,257
You tell the Guardians
any of this?

868
00:46:42,341 --> 00:46:44,260
(BIRD CHIRPING)

869
00:46:44,802 --> 00:46:46,137
JOHN: I report to you.

870
00:46:47,972 --> 00:46:49,515
- Hey.
- What?

871
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,560
HAL:
What's with that bird, anyway?

872
00:46:52,601 --> 00:46:53,602
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

873
00:46:53,686 --> 00:46:55,438
- What are you talking about?
- The bird.

874
00:46:55,521 --> 00:46:57,398
I mean, you brought it to life
with your subconscious.

875
00:46:57,481 --> 00:46:59,442
It must mean
something pretty deep.

876
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:00,609
It's just a bird.

877
00:47:01,777 --> 00:47:04,613
(CHIRPS)

878
00:47:05,239 --> 00:47:06,449
(CONSTRUCT WARBLES)

879
00:47:12,121 --> 00:47:16,751
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

880
00:47:16,792 --> 00:47:20,880
(DOOR OPENS, CLOSES)

881
00:47:24,008 --> 00:47:27,094
♪ (FAST-TEMPO
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

882
00:47:31,349 --> 00:47:32,433
(LANTERN CLANGS)

883
00:47:46,322 --> 00:47:49,116
♪ (DRAMATIC
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

884
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:01,670
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

885
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:22,233
(CLANGING HUM)

886
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:25,653
(CLANGING HUM)

887
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:30,324
(DOOR HUMS)

888
00:48:30,366 --> 00:48:32,243
- Authorize Hal Jordan.
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

889
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:33,619
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Access granted.</i>

890
00:48:35,788 --> 00:48:38,791
(CELL DOOR WHIRRING)

891
00:48:54,890 --> 00:48:55,891
Sinestro.

892
00:48:57,560 --> 00:48:58,561
Hal.

893
00:49:00,146 --> 00:49:01,939
Tell me what you know
about Manhunters.

894
00:49:02,022 --> 00:49:03,691
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
BY PRETTY SICK PLAYING) ♪

895
00:49:03,732 --> 00:49:06,777
No hello?
No how have I been?

896
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,655
HAL: Hello, Sinestro,
how have you been?

897
00:49:11,115 --> 00:49:13,242
Now, what the fuck do you know
about Manhunters?

898
00:49:14,577 --> 00:49:16,162
If one still existed,

899
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,539
it'd be the second
greatest threat

900
00:49:18,581 --> 00:49:19,915
you're currently facing.

901
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:23,836
So why don't you tell me
about John Stewart?

902
00:49:23,878 --> 00:49:26,797
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
CONTINUES PLAYING) ♪

903
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:34,597
<i>♪ She takes my hand
And she pours me a glass ♪</i>

904
00:49:34,680 --> 00:49:36,891
<i>♪ Addiction's a disease
So, I get a pass ♪</i>

905
00:49:36,974 --> 00:49:42,563
<i>♪ I wanna feel something again ♪</i>

906
00:49:42,605 --> 00:49:45,232
<i>♪ She takes my hand
And she asks me to dance ♪</i>

907
00:49:45,274 --> 00:49:47,401
<i>♪ Nothing really matters
If you don't have romance ♪</i>

908
00:49:47,485 --> 00:49:53,407
<i>♪ I wanna feel something again ♪</i>

909
00:50:03,792 --> 00:50:05,920
<i>♪ He takes me out and says
"Let's do business" ♪</i>

910
00:50:05,961 --> 00:50:08,589
<i>♪ He's a bad guy
But I believe in forgiveness ♪</i>

911
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:12,968
<i>♪ I wanna do something
That matters ♪</i>

912
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:16,305
<i>♪ Takes a meeting
'Cause he likes my vision ♪</i>

913
00:50:16,388 --> 00:50:19,016
<i>♪ I'm not opportunistic
No, I'm just ambitious ♪</i>

914
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:24,980
<i>♪ I wanna be someone
That matters ♪</i>

915
00:50:45,251 --> 00:50:47,670
<i>♪ The freedom you're being sold
Is just submission ♪</i>

916
00:50:47,753 --> 00:50:50,506
<i>♪ They wanna keep you content
And under supervision ♪</i>

917
00:50:50,589 --> 00:50:53,050
<i>♪ They got you convinced
That ignorance is bliss in ♪</i>

918
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:56,345
<i>♪ Some ever changing mind
Erasing human condition ♪</i>

919
00:50:56,428 --> 00:51:02,017
<i>♪ I don't have time
To worry about ♪</i>

920
00:51:02,101 --> 00:51:07,106
<i>♪ If I am stuck
And if there's any way out ♪</i>

921
00:51:07,189 --> 00:51:12,319
<i>♪ I don't have time ♪</i>

922
00:51:12,403 --> 00:51:17,449
<i>♪ I don't have time ♪</i>

923
00:51:18,909 --> 00:51:20,536
♪ (SONG CONCLUDES) ♪

